==Battleground==
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 16.67~33.33 seconds<sup>500f~1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Pigge]]s spawn, delay 33.33~50 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,500f</sup>.
*3 [[Zigge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 3.33~10 seconds<sup>100f~300f</sup>.
*4 [[Zoge]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 30~40 seconds<sup>900f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Lowkey]] spawns as the boss.
**2 [[Coffin Zoge]]s spawn, delay 30 seconds<sup>900f</sup>.
**4 [[Zory|Zories]] spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**6 [[Zroco]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
**6 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The important thing is to just outlast the horde of Zombies: once you've done this, you can chip away Lowkey's health with a cat that outranges it, like [[Li'l Nyandam (Special Cat)|Li'l Nyandam]]. You want around 3 meatshields, a general AoE attacker ([[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]],) and zombie killers ([[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pole Vaulter]], [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]], or [[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Awakened Musashi]].) [[Welterweight Cat (Rare Cat)|Welterweight Cat]] can play a fairly crucial role in keeping the Zories from pushing super hard and can make your life a lot easier. For the actual gameplay, just build up a wall of cats in the beginning and don't lure: the zombie horde will probably push you at least halfway to your base, and the Lowkey is not as large a threat as the Zories.

